PROBLEM STATEMENT:
You are given a string s of even length.
Split it into two halves:
a = first half
b = second half
Two strings are alike if they contain the same number of vowels (a, e, i, o, u, A, E, I, O, U).
Return true if a and b are alike, otherwise return false
JAVA CODE:
import java.util.*;

class Solution {
    public boolean halvesAreAlike(String s) {
        int n = s.length();
        int mid = n / 2;
        
        String vowels = "aeiouAEIOU";
        int countA = 0, countB = 0;
        
        for (int i = 0; i < mid; i++) {
            if (vowels.indexOf(s.charAt(i)) != -1) countA++;
        }
        for (int i = mid; i < n; i++) {
            if (vowels.indexOf(s.charAt(i)) != -1) countB++;
        }
        
        return countA == countB;
    }
}
INPUT:
s = "textbook"
OUTPUT:
false
